    "title": "White County Trail Rangers Participate In 3rd Expedition - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dean Dyer ,\n18 hours ago (Cleveland)- This past weekend, the White County Trail Rangers traveled to the tiny town of Jackson, Georgia, to ride the trails at Dauset Nature Preserve. Dauset Nature Preserve is home to many animals who are not able to be released into the wild after being rescued, including Georgia’s infamous weather predictor himself, General Lee the groundhog. Dauset Trails was hit by awful flooding last year and has worked extremely hard to have the trails in top shape for the Trail Rangers’ return, and they did not disappoint. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
